    on the Abridged BDB by Online Bible (Larry Pierce); TBESG's on Abbott-Smith.
Changes made by COTEXT: the data is reformatted into one SQLite database; morphology codes are converted into
COTEXT's own codes and spelled out; glosses lose their segment marks; lexicon entries keep only bold, italic and
line breaks.

Grammars (the word's panel links each term of a parsing to its section):
  - Gesenius' Hebrew Grammar, edited and enlarged by E. Kautzsch, translated by A. E. Cowley (2nd English edition,
    Oxford, 1910): public domain. Text from the English Wikisource transcription (en.wikisource.org, "Gesenius'
    Hebrew Grammar"), at the page revisions listed in pipeline/gesenius_revisions.json.
  - Herbert Weir Smyth, A Greek Grammar for Colleges (American Book Company, 1920): the Perseus Digital Library's
    edition (Perseus:text:1999.04.0007), Trustees of Tufts University, licensed CC BY-SA 3.0 US
    (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/us/). Its sections as they're kept in COTEXT's database (the
    grammar_sections table, Smyth's rows) are shared under the same licence.
  Changes made by COTEXT: the sections are reduced to paragraphs, bold, italics, tables and footnotes; Smyth's Greek
  is converted from Beta Code to Unicode; Gesenius' Bible references are written out from the transcription's
  templates; bibliographic tags are dropped.

